                "annotations": [],
                "text": "An analysis of the training examples reveals the following rule:\n\n1. Let $K$ be the number of non-zero cells in the top row, and $C$ be their color. Let $W$ be the width of the input grid.\n2. Form a 1D sequence of runs of color $C$ separated by a single `0`. The run lengths increase from $1$ up to $K$, then decrease back down to $1$ (i.e. lengths: $1, 2, \\dots, K, \\dots, 2, 1$).\n3. The total length of this pattern is $K^2 + 2(K - 1)$.\n4. Wrap this 1D sequence into rows of width $W$, requiring $H = \\lceil (K^2 + 2K - 2) / W \\rceil$ rows.\n5. Pad any remaining cells at the end of the last row with `0`s.\n\nPlease provide the test input to generate the solution.",
